}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Blue Nyanko Ranger''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
This Cat is a spammable anti-[[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] DPS unit that faces heavy competition from other Cats, namely [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]. Blue Nyanko Ranger's primary advantage lies in their gargantuan standing range when compared to most cats of their kind; however, in practice, this range advantage is hardly notable. Most common Red enemies are melee attackers, which other [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red cats]] like Courier Cat or [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]] can easily outrange (or tank), making Blue Nyanko Ranger's range inconsequential outside of problematic mixed stages with midranged enemies. Other dangerous Red enemies, such as [[Professor A.]], [[Raynard]], or [[Two Can]], either outrange this cat, or have abilities that let them hit Blue Nyanko Ranger from a large effective distance, rendering their standing range pointless. They ultimately fall short of Courier Cat's likeness in every regard due to the latter's piercing attacks, spammability, and superior DPS.

Despite Blue Nyanko Ranger's underwhelming performance as an attacker, they do have a use in their powerful Research Power XL [[Cat Combo|Combo]] that can reduce the long recharge rates of the other [[:Category:Nyanko Rangers|Nyanko Rangers]] as well as its own. This does not work for non-Ranger units, but it may be worth bringing this unit for their Combo alone if using other Nyanko Rangers. Additionally, [[Helmet Cat (Special Cat)|Yellow Nyanko Ranger]]'s Cat Combo can provide Blue Nyanko Ranger with Wave Immunity, which gives them a niche as an attacker against Two Can and [[Berserkory]] in {{4c}} restriction stages where most [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shields]] are not available.

Overall, this Cat is mainly useful in the early-game before unlocking other powerful anti-Red attackers, in the [[Underground Labyrinth]] as a Courier sidegrade, or to reduce the recharge of other Nyanko Rangers. While Blue Nyanko Ranger isn't bad per se, there is little reason to use them over their alternatives.

